   "evidence": "At head, codex.ts:814-823 wraps tool-enabled calls in runSandboxed(opts, roots(), ...). The roots are writeRoots(cwd, scratch) for editors and {write:[scratch]} for readers, and the env is agentEnv(scratchEnv(spec)), where scratchEnv sets only TMPDIR/TMP/TEMP. CODEX_HOME is not redirected, and --ephemeral is added only for privateSession (codex.ts:682). seatbeltProfile denies file-write* outside the roots. At base, Codex ran through processRunner with no outer profile. The Claude adapter handles the same issue by making every tool-enabled invocation ephemeral, as the research doc explains. Codex got no such accommodation, and the codex-cli run here shows it cannot start with a read-only CODEX_HOME. This mechanism (state-folder writes denied) is separate from G1 (nested sandbox_apply refused), though both stop tool-enabled Codex from starting."
