   "evidence": "HEAD adds runSandboxed around every tool-enabled Codex invocation. Its roots permit writes only to scratch and, for editors, the checkout. seatbeltProfile declares `(deny file-write*)` before granting those roots. However, the invocation still uses `env: agentEnv(scratchEnv(spec))`; scratchEnv overrides only TMPDIR, TMP and TEMP, preserving HOME/CODEX_HOME. buildCodexArgs adds --ephemeral only for privateSession. Base launched the same persistent CLI directly without this outer write restriction. The offline permission probe independently reproduced the initialization failure without network access. Full production Seatbelt integration is unreproduced because this worker rejects even a permissive nested sandbox. This is a runtime-state write failure, distinct from G1's nested-sandbox initialization failure."
